# PSEO / SEO safety (Smetoplan)

Long-tail PSEO is a growth channel, but **safety beats volume**.

## Forbidden
- Thin / doorway pages (same calc, different intent verbs: raschet/smeta/online clones)
- Phantom cities / missing `region_slug`
- Pages without reinforcement params when structure needs rebar
- Bulk `UPDATE … SET is_published = TRUE` bypassing the gate
- Publishing without unique `paramsFingerprint` + safe SSR snapshot (FAQ ≥6, real volumes)
- Cron bursts of 200–300+/day without explicit ops decision

## Required
- Single intent cluster: `kalkulyator` (gate rejects `doorway_intent`)
- Canonical regions only (moskva, spb, krasnodar, ekaterinburg, novosibirsk)
- Every indexable URL passes `evaluatePseoIndexability` (used by drip, sitemap, `[slug]`)
- **Live calc bridge:** SSR numbers come ONLY from `buildPseoSnapshot` → `calculateMaterials`. DB stores params, never frozen volumes. Kernel fixes (formwork, rebar, strip axis…) automatically update every leaf on next request.
- Live calc must yield `concreteVolumeM3 > 0` and useful rebar/BOM
- Drip-feed only (`pseo:drip` / cron defaults 40–80/day) — never thousands overnight
- After gate tighten: run `pseo:remediate` before growing the index
- Guard with `tests/golden/pseo-live-engine.test.ts` when changing geometry/rebar
## Commands
- Dry-run gate+calc: `npm run pseo:verify-corpus`
- Upsert drafts: `npm run db:generate-pseo`
- Spot-check live index: `npm run pseo:spotcheck`
- Unpublish unsafe: `npm run pseo:remediate`
- Publish batch: `npm run pseo:drip` or `npm run pseo:publish-safe`
